From: Armada <no-reply@armadaos.dev>
Subject: [PATCH] tu: render shared UBWC attachments in GMEM

In Lepton on Armada, Android's gralloc buffers are UBWC and the host scans
them out directly. Frames SurfaceFlinger renders into them through zink
with sysmem rendering may scan out with small black blocks in random places.
The GPU reads the same buffers back correctly, so gamescope screenshots and
forced composition look fine.

Use GMEM for render passes with an imported UBWC attachment
(DRM_FORMAT_MOD_QCOM_COMPRESSED) whenever GMEM is possible.
---
diff --git a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_cmd_buffer.cc b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_cmd_buffer.cc
--- a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_cmd_buffer.cc
+++ b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_cmd_buffer.cc
@@ -9,6 +9,8 @@
 
 #include "tu_cmd_buffer.h"
 
+#include "drm-uapi/drm_fourcc.h"
+
 #include "vk_common_entrypoints.h"
 #include "vk_log.h"
 #include "vk_render_pass.h"
@@ -1481,6 +1483,19 @@ use_sysmem_rendering(struct tu_cmd_buffer *cmd,
       return false;
    }
 
+   /* The display engine reads imported UBWC buffers directly. What sysmem
+    * rendering leaves in them scans out with black blocks on some devices,
+    * while GMEM resolves display correctly.
+    */
+   for (unsigned a = 0; a < cmd->state.pass->attachment_count; a++) {
+      const struct tu_image_view *iview = cmd->state.attachments[a];
+      if (iview && iview->image->layout[0].ubwc &&
+          iview->image->vk.drm_format_mod == DRM_FORMAT_MOD_QCOM_COMPRESSED) {
+         cmd->state.rp.force_render_mode_reason = "Shared UBWC attachment";
+         return false;
+      }
+   }
+
    /* This is a case where it's better to avoid GMEM, too many tiles but no HW binning possible. */
    if (!vsc->binning_possible && vsc->binning_useful) {
       cmd->state.rp.force_render_mode_reason =
